Interpret modified growth and decay.
The following scenarios all have a limiting value;
They have the differential equation where k < 0:
\frac{dQ}{dt}=k(Q-P);\qquad Q=P+Ae^{kt}

entries.expectedAnswer:
P = 2000 + Ae^{kt}
dP/dt = Ake^{kt}
k(P − 2000) = k(Ae^{kt}) = Ake^{kt}

T = 3 + Ae^{kt}
dT/dt = kAe^{kt}
k(T − 3) = k(3 + Ae^{kt} − 3) = k(Ae^{kt}) = kAe^{kt}
